<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>

    <!-- dotnet tool install -g Roslynaut. The package holds the publish output, so the helper hosts beside the server too. -->
    <PackAsTool>true</PackAsTool>
    <ToolCommandName>roslynaut</ToolCommandName>
    <RollForward>Major</RollForward>
    <Version>0.3.0</Version>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
- --install and --uninstall take more agents: codex (Codex CLI, IDE extension and app, in ~/.codex/config.toml or under CODEX_HOME, with a tool timeout of 30 minutes for builds and tests), vscode (the user profile's mcp.json), visualstudio (~/.mcp.json), copilot (GitHub Copilot CLI, in ~/.copilot/mcp-config.json or under COPILOT_HOME), cursor (~/.cursor/mcp.json), gemini (Gemini CLI, ~/.gemini/settings.json) and junie (~/.junie/mcp/mcp.json). They get the MCP server for all projects, without a hook.
- --install codex edits config.toml in place, keeping the rest of the file, comments included.
- The README describes running Roslynaut through dnx, without installing the tool, where dotnet tool install -g fails.
- process_cpu, process_allocations and process_events take trace: a .nettrace file recorded earlier, such as by dotnet-trace collect on CI or another machine, to analyze instead of tracing a process.
- diagnostics takes aot: the trim, native AOT and single-file warnings (IL2xxx, IL3xxx) that PublishTrimmed or PublishAot would give, without changing the project or publishing.
- verify_pending lists the snapshots Verify tests received with their diffs from the verified ones, and accepts or rejects them.
- regex_test runs a .NET regular expression against sample inputs, with each match's groups and the result of a replacement, without evaluate.
- resources checks .resx files against their translations (resources a culture lacks or only it has) and finds the resources no C# code uses.
- The Claude Code and OpenCode hooks suggest resources for .resx files and verify_pending for received snapshots and after dotnet test.
- diagnostics with analyzerPackages loads packages whose analyzers are not in a roslyn* folder, where it failed with "Sequence contains no elements".
- The package is precompiled (ReadyToRun) for Windows, Linux and macOS on x64 and Arm64, so the server starts and answers its first calls sooner. It comes as a package per platform, which dotnet tool install and dnx pick, and a framework-dependent one for other platforms.
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Authors>Wesley Baartman</Authors>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 Wesley Baartman</Copyright>
    <Description>An MCP server that exposes Roslyn and MSBuild to agents: navigation, analysis, refactoring, builds and tests, IL/JIT disassembly, decompilation, process inspection and debugging of C# projects.</Description>
    <PackageTags>mcp;roslyn;msbuild;csharp;agents;opencode;claude;llm;agentic</PackageTags>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/CptWesley/Roslynaut</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/CptWesley/Roslynaut</RepositoryUrl>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Release precompiles the server and its dependencies, which spares the JIT time of Roslyn, MSBuild and the rest on each start.
       ReadyToRun code is for one platform: dotnet pack makes a package per runtime, a framework-dependent one for the others (any), and
       the package Roslynaut that points the tool's install at the right one. -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)' == 'Release'">
    <RuntimeIdentifiers>win-x64;win-arm64;linux-x64;linux-arm64;linux-musl-x64;linux-musl-arm64;osx-x64;osx-arm64;any</RuntimeIdentifiers>
    <PublishReadyToRun>true</PublishReadyToRun>
    <!-- With an app host, the tool's command would launch it by its path in the tool store, which changes with every version, and
         --install would register that path; on Windows the command would also be a .cmd, which Node.js cannot start without a shell. -->
    <UseAppHost>false</UseAppHost>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Roslynaut.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Buildalyzer" Version="9.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="ICSharpCode.Decompiler" Version="11.1.0.9782" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp.Features" Version="5.9.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp.Workspaces" Version="5.9.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.VisualBasic.Workspaces" Version="5.9.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Diagnostics.NETCore.Client" Version="0.2.750501" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Diagnostics.Runtime" Version="4.2.751201" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Diagnostics.Tracing.TraceEvent" Version="3.2.5" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection" Version="10.0.13" />
    <PackageReference Include="ModelContextProtocol.AspNetCore" Version="2.2.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Mono.Cecil" Version="0.11.6" />
    <PackageReference Include="MSBuild.StructuredLogger" Version="2.3.246" />
    <PackageReference Include="NuGet.Credentials" Version="7.9.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="NuGet.ProjectModel" Version="7.9.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="NuGet.Protocol" Version="7.9.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.CommandLine" Version="2.0.14" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Security.Cryptography.Xml" Version="10.0.13" />
    <PackageReference Include="Tomlyn" Version="2.11.1" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Roslynaut.CallCounter\Roslynaut.CallCounter.csproj" GlobalPropertiesToRemove="RuntimeIdentifier;SelfContained" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Roslynaut.JitHost\Roslynaut.JitHost.csproj" GlobalPropertiesToRemove="RuntimeIdentifier;SelfContained" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Roslynaut.ScriptHost\Roslynaut.ScriptHost.csproj" GlobalPropertiesToRemove="RuntimeIdentifier;SelfContained" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
